---
import PublicationPage from '../layouts/PublicationPage.astro';
import { categories } from '../lib/config';
import { getAllPosts } from '../lib/posts';

const posts = await getAllPosts();
---
<PublicationPage title="About ServerHi" description="ServerHi publishes Linux administration guides, container walkthroughs and operational notes on releases and advisories.">
  <h2>Browse the publication</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/archive/">archive</a> contains {posts.length} published articles. Choose a subject to find its guides and dated reports.</p>
  <ul>
    {categories.map(category => (
      <li>
        <a href={`/category/${category.slug}/`}>{category.name}</a>
        {' — '}{posts.filter(post => post.data.category === category.slug).length} articles.
        {' '}{category.description}.
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <h2>How to read a guide</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/posts/backup-strategies/">database recovery walkthrough</a> restores a known record and checks specific failure cases. Our <a href="/posts/ubuntu-26-04-lts-preview/">Ubuntu release guide</a> traces release and upgrade claims to Canonical. Look for the environment, date and source attached to the particular claim.</p>
  <h2>Who publishes it</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/author/">ServerHi editorial byline</a> identifies the publication responsible for the articles. Our <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> explains how to read test results and report corrections.</p>
</PublicationPage>
